# Cisco Bulk Hash File signature-verification certificate (pinned).
#
# This is Cisco's own end-entity X.509 certificate for verifying the
# detached signature ("<name>.csv.signature") shipped alongside the Bulk
# Hash CSV -- server/bulkhash.py's verify_tar() checks a downloaded feed's
# signature against ONLY this pinned copy; it never trusts a certificate
# extracted from the downloaded tar itself. Any failure to verify keeps the
# prior verdicts untouched (fail-closed) -- see the reconciler's docstring.
#
# Provenance:
#   Source: https://tools.cisco.com/cscrdr/security/center/files/trust/Cisco_BulkHash_CSV.tar
#           (302-redirects to cscrdr.cloudapps.cisco.com; no login wall)
#   Fetched: 2026-08-29 (live download of the tar, this file extracted from
#            it -- original member name inside the bundle:
#            KNOWNGOODVALUESPROD-CCO_RELEASE.cer)
#   Subject: CN=KnownGoodValuesPROD, OU=REL, O=Cisco
#   Issuer:  O=Cisco, CN=Innerspace SubCA RSA
#   Validity: notBefore=2016-08-26 17:56:56 GMT, notAfter=2037-11-11 17:56:56 GMT
#   SHA-256 fingerprint (of the DER bytes): cc84840e9d8a1e31c30cbca9b87e870bfd350bd13a5240165c766e9dae964c59
#
# Authenticity check performed at fetch time (2026-08-29), mirroring Cisco's
# own cisco_x509_verify_release.py verification recipe:
#   1. Downloaded Cisco's published root (crcam2.cer) and SubCA
#      (innerspace.cer) certs from http://www.cisco.com/security/pki/certs/
#      and confirmed their SHA-256 hashes match the values hardcoded in
#      Cisco's own verify script (root: cd85167b3935e27bcc3b0f5fa24c8457882d0bb994f88269a7f72829d957eae9,
#      subca: f31e6b39dae6996fdf2045a61be8bd3688a86dfd06c46ce71af4af239f411c56).
#   2. `openssl verify -CAfile crcam2.pem -untrusted innerspace.cer
#      KNOWNGOODVALUESPROD-CCO_RELEASE.cer` -> OK (full 3-tier chain valid).
#   3. `openssl dgst -sha512 -verify <pubkey from this cert> -signature
#      Cisco_BulkHash_CSV.csv.signature Cisco_BulkHash_CSV.csv` -> "Verified
#      OK" against the real, live feed downloaded the same day.
#
# Recipe this module implements (matches Cisco's cisco_x509_verify_release.py3,
# `-v dgst -sha512` mode): extract the public key from this certificate via
# `openssl x509 -pubkey -noout`, then `openssl dgst -sha512 -verify <pubkey>
# -signature <detached-signature> <csv-bytes>`.
